  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The diagonals of a rhombus have lengths 6 and 8. Find the height corresponding to one side of the rhombus. (Write the result as a decimal.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4.8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The diagonals bisect each other at right angles, so a side is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs \\(6/2=3\\) and \\(8/2=4\\). The side length is therefore \\(\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5\\), and the area is \\(6\\times8\\div2=24\\). Using area = side length × height, the height is \\(24\\div5=4.8\\).",
